To set up FastAPI with SQLModel and PostgreSQL, you will use SQLModel (which combines SQLAlchemy ORM and Pydantic validation) alongside psycopg2-binary (or asyncpg for async setups) as the PostgreSQL driver.
1. Install Required Packages
First, activate your virtual environment and install fastapi, sqlmodel, and the PostgreSQL driver (psycopg2-binary for synchronous operations or asyncpg for asynchronous operations):
# Standard sync setup
pip install "fastapi[standard]" sqlmodel psycopg2-binary

2. Configure Database Connection (app/database.py)
Create app/database.py to hold your database URL, engine setup, session dependency, and lifecycle table initialization.
from typing import Generator
from sqlmodel import SQLModel, Session, create_engine

# Connection string: postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/dbname
POSTGRES_URL = "postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/my_db"

engine = create_engine(POSTGRES_URL, echo=True)

def create_db_and_tables():
    """Creates database tables on startup based on SQLModel metadata."""
    SQLModel.metadata.create_all(engine)

def get_session() -> Generator[Session, None, None]:
    """Dependency yielding a database session for request handling."""
    with Session(engine) as session:
        yield session

3. Define Database Models (app/models.py)
Define your database schema using SQLModel. The table=True argument registers the class as a database table.
from typing import Optional
from sqlmodel import SQLModel, Field

# Database Table Schema
class Item(SQLModel, table=True):
    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)
    title: str = Field(index=True)
    description: Optional[str] = None
    price: float
    is_available: bool = True

# Pydantic Schemas for Request/Response Validation
class ItemCreate(SQLModel):
    title: str
    description: Optional[str] = None
    price: float
    is_available: bool = True

class ItemRead(SQLModel):
    id: int
    title: str
    description: Optional[str] = None
    price: float
    is_available: bool

4. Create API Endpoints (app/main.py)
Use FastAPI's lifespan context manager to handle automatic table creation when the application starts, and inject the Session dependency into your routes.
from contextlib import asynccontextmanager
from typing import List
from fastapi import FastAPI, Depends, HTTPException, status
from sqlmodel import Session, select

from app.database import create_db_and_tables, get_session
from app.models import Item, ItemCreate, ItemRead

@asynccontextmanager
async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):
    # Setup tables on startup
    create_db_and_tables()
    yield

app = FastAPI(title="FastAPI + SQLModel + PostgreSQL", lifespan=lifespan)

@app.post("/items/", response_model=ItemRead, status_code=status.HTTP_201_CREATED)
def create_item(item: ItemCreate, session: Session = Depends(get_session)):
    # Convert Pydantic request data to DB Model
    db_item = Item.model_validate(item)
    session.add(db_item)
    session.commit()
    session.refresh(db_item)
    return db_item

@app.get("/items/", response_model=List[ItemRead])
def read_items(offset: int = 0, limit: int = 100, session: Session = Depends(get_session)):
    statement = select(Item).offset(offset).limit(limit)
    items = session.exec(statement).all()
    return items

@app.get("/items/{item_id}", response_model=ItemRead)
def read_item(item_id: int, session: Session = Depends(get_session)):
    item = session.get(Item, item_id)
    if not item:
        raise HTTPException(status_code=404, detail="Item not found")
    return item

5. Run the Server
Start your PostgreSQL database instance, make sure the database my_db exists, then run your FastAPI application:
fastapi dev app/main.py

Check [http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs) to test interactive CRUD requests directly against your PostgreSQL database.
